It all started when our teacher randomly rearranged the seating chart and placed us together. Honestly, I had no big expectations—you already had a best friend back then, so I kept my distance and never intended to come between you two. But as the days turned into months, sitting side by side slowly broke down all our walls. We started sharing quiet laughs, helping each other with class concepts, and getting comfortable in a way I never saw coming. By the time Class 8 ended and Class 9 began, so many things around us had shifted, but our bond only grew stronger.
Looking back, if your former best friend Aarti hadn't grown distant from you, I often wonder—would we have ever become this close? I don't know if how things unfolded was good or bad for you, but selfishly, for me, it was the absolute best thing that could have ever happened.</p>
